  "question": {
    "text": "If the normal to the curve $y=f(x)$ at the point $(3,4)$ make an angle $3 \\pi / 4$ with the positive $x$-axis, then $f(3)$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "1",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "-1",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-\\frac{3}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $\\frac{d y}{d x}=f^{\\prime}(x)$, Slope of normal $=-\\frac{1}{f^{\\prime}(x)},-\\frac{1}{f^{\\prime}(3)}=\\tan \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}=-1$ $f^{\\prime}(3)=1$"
  }
